00:01:54.314 --> 00:01:55.849
He goes to community college

00:01:55.849 --> 00:01:56.983
and gets start

00:01:56.983 --> 00:01:58.651
studying psychology and starts

00:01:58.651 --> 00:02:01.054
messaging other friends about saying he's

00:02:01.054 --> 00:02:02.722
he's interested in studying

00:02:02.722 --> 00:02:03.690
the minds of criminals.

00:02:03.690 --> 00:02:05.592
It seems like he's found a passion

00:02:05.592 --> 00:02:06.826
of some kind

00:02:06.826 --> 00:02:09.762
in psychology and criminology.

00:02:10.163 --> 00:02:10.864
Wow.

00:02:11.598 --> 00:02:12.665
And then he ends up going

00:02:12.665 --> 00:02:13.233
of course, as we

00:02:13.233 --> 00:02:15.034
now to across the country

00:02:15.034 --> 00:02:15.768
from Pennsylvania,

00:02:15.768 --> 00:02:17.670
where he grew up to Washington state

00:02:17.670 --> 00:02:19.706
last summer and starts a Ph.D.

00:02:19.706 --> 00:02:21.541
program in criminology there.

00:02:21.541 --> 00:02:23.476
So it's amazing to see this.

00:02:23.476 --> 00:02:24.110
And you've had a chance

00:02:24.110 --> 00:02:25.378
to read all through this,

00:02:25.378 --> 00:02:26.412
which which has to be

00:02:27.480 --> 00:02:28.381
difficult.

00:02:28.381 --> 00:02:30.450
You say that one of his friends

00:02:30.450 --> 00:02:31.217
told you

00:02:31.217 --> 00:02:32.185
that coworker suffered

00:02:32.185 --> 00:02:33.553
from a neurological condition

00:02:33.553 --> 00:02:34.420
called a visual

00:02:34.420 --> 00:02:36.723
snow, where people basically,

00:02:36.723 --> 00:02:38.458
as you describe it, see scattered

00:02:38.458 --> 00:02:40.026
dots like sort of static

00:02:40.026 --> 00:02:41.561
on a on a television

00:02:41.561 --> 00:02:43.863
to people of a certain age.

00:02:43.863 --> 00:02:45.965
One of the posts you shared with us

00:02:46.232 --> 00:02:47.901
says, and I quote,

00:02:47.901 --> 00:02:49.135
What you shared with us

00:02:49.135 --> 00:02:50.603
is as if the ringing in my ears

00:02:50.603 --> 00:02:51.604
and the fuzz in my vision

00:02:51.604 --> 00:02:53.640
is simply all the demons in my head

00:02:54.007 --> 00:02:55.742
mocking me.

00:02:55.742 --> 00:02:56.776
What else

00:02:56.776 --> 00:02:59.946
do you know about the context there?

00:03:00.079 --> 00:03:02.649
Yeah, the visual snow is a really

00:03:02.682 --> 00:03:04.117
little understood condition.

00:03:04.117 --> 00:03:05.084
It's like you said, it's

00:03:05.084 --> 00:03:06.920
static in your vision,

00:03:06.920 --> 00:03:08.188
like old television.

00:03:08.188 --> 00:03:10.089
And it

00:03:10.089 --> 00:03:10.690
there's really

00:03:10.690 --> 00:03:13.493
the causes still not fully clear,

00:03:13.760 --> 00:03:15.328
but it really can be debilitating

00:03:15.328 --> 00:03:16.763
for some people.

00:03:16.763 --> 00:03:17.630
You know, I want to be clear.

00:03:17.630 --> 00:03:19.832
It's not a sign of mental illness

00:03:19.832 --> 00:03:20.900
and it's not something

00:03:20.900 --> 00:03:21.935
that anyone has said

00:03:21.935 --> 00:03:23.636
could explain

00:03:23.636 --> 00:03:25.772
these these heinous killings.

00:03:27.006 --> 00:03:28.208
But it's something that

00:03:28.208 --> 00:03:29.075
he complained a lot

00:03:29.075 --> 00:03:30.610
about as a teenager, both to friends

00:03:30.610 --> 00:03:32.345
and on these online posts.

00:03:32.345 --> 00:03:33.813
And that was coupled with

00:03:33.813 --> 00:03:36.216
his complaints about life in general.

00:03:36.216 --> 00:03:36.416
All right.

00:03:36.416 --> 00:03:37.617
Well, Nick, thank you very much.

00:03:37.617 --> 00:03:39.452
I appreciate your sharing

00:03:39.452 --> 00:03:40.420
your reporting with us

00:03:40.420 --> 00:03:41.854
and some of those posts is disturbing

00:03:41.854 --> 00:03:42.589
as they are as people

00:03:42.589 --> 00:03:43.856
try to understand this.

00:03:43.856 --> 00:03:44.490
Thank you.

00:03:44.490 --> 00:03:45.625
And on the back of Nick's

00:03:45.625 --> 00:03:47.393
reporting, let's now bring in Jim Fallon.

00:03:47.393 --> 00:03:48.394
He's a neuroscientist

00:03:48.394 --> 00:03:50.163
and professor of psychiatry

00:03:50.163 --> 00:03:52.332
and human behavior at UC Irvine.

00:03:52.332 --> 00:03:54.934
So, Jim, you know, you hear Nick,

00:03:55.168 --> 00:03:56.469
The New York Times reporter

00:03:56.469 --> 00:03:58.404
talking about Coburg are suffering

00:03:58.404 --> 00:04:00.506
from a condition called visual snow

00:04:00.506 --> 00:04:01.341
and the Times,

00:04:01.341 --> 00:04:02.342
as he referenced

00:04:02.342 --> 00:04:04.444
this with the initials V.

00:04:04.444 --> 00:04:06.579
S in an online post

00:04:06.846 --> 00:04:08.448
that says, when I get home,

00:04:08.448 --> 00:04:09.649
I mean, to my family,

00:04:09.649 --> 00:04:11.751
this started when voice did

00:04:11.751 --> 00:04:14.087
I felt no emotion.

00:04:14.087 --> 00:04:14.621
Is there anything

00:04:14.621 --> 00:04:15.788
you can tell us about this

00:04:15.788 --> 00:04:17.924
visual snow condition?

00:04:19.792 --> 00:04:20.493
Well, the visual

00:04:20.493 --> 00:04:23.029
snow is often associated with migraine.

00:04:24.330 --> 00:04:26.799
And it's it's thought to be generated

00:04:26.799 --> 00:04:29.669
by hyper stimulated neurons.

00:04:30.270 --> 00:04:31.638
The base of the temporal lobe.

00:04:31.638 --> 00:04:33.206
That's where visual processing,

00:04:33.206 --> 00:04:35.642
a lot of visual processing occurs.

00:04:36.743 --> 00:04:38.845
And so, yes, it's it's

00:04:38.845 --> 00:04:39.946
debilitating and almost

00:04:39.946 --> 00:04:42.215
nothing is known about it.

00:04:42.215 --> 00:04:45.218
But it is a

00:04:45.218 --> 00:04:47.020
syndrome

00:04:47.654 --> 00:04:50.189
that you know, it's

00:04:50.189 --> 00:04:50.523
you know,

00:04:50.523 --> 00:04:51.658
you never hear about it

00:04:51.658 --> 00:04:53.026
being associated with murder

00:04:53.026 --> 00:04:54.394
or anything like that.

00:04:54.394 --> 00:04:57.196
Although if you read the rest of his post

00:04:58.331 --> 00:05:00.500
and it seems clear

00:05:00.500 --> 00:05:01.167
that he's got

00:05:01.167 --> 00:05:03.169
a depersonalization syndrome

00:05:04.270 --> 00:05:07.340
and which is a dissociative disorder,

00:05:07.340 --> 00:05:10.009
where you feel separated from yourself.

00:05:10.910 --> 00:05:13.413
And is that when you're talking about,

00:05:13.413 --> 00:05:14.280
as Nick was just saying,

00:05:14.280 --> 00:05:14.447
you know,

00:05:14.447 --> 00:05:15.715
sort of when he looks at the faces

00:05:15.715 --> 00:05:16.783
of his family members,

00:05:16.783 --> 00:05:18.284
he just says he feels nothing.

00:05:18.284 --> 00:05:20.653
Is that that's what you're referring to?

00:05:22.722 --> 00:05:23.289
Well, yes.

00:05:23.289 --> 00:05:24.424
You know, you have

00:05:24.424 --> 00:05:26.392
on the top of your head right here

00:05:26.392 --> 00:05:28.227
in the spiritual parietal cortex.

00:05:28.227 --> 00:05:30.063
You have a GPS system.

00:05:30.063 --> 00:05:32.031
But what it does is it puts together

00:05:32.031 --> 00:05:33.232
your whole world.

00:05:33.232 --> 00:05:35.234
It tells you where your eyes are,

00:05:35.234 --> 00:05:36.936
relationship to your head,

00:05:36.936 --> 00:05:39.105
but relationship to the world.

00:05:39.105 --> 00:05:41.341
And then it adds an emotion to that.

00:05:41.641 --> 00:05:43.343
And all of that apparatus

00:05:43.343 --> 00:05:45.411
seems to be damaged.

00:05:45.411 --> 00:05:46.679
And so

00:05:46.679 --> 00:05:48.815
he doesn't even connect with himself.

00:05:49.115 --> 00:05:50.850
So he doesn't even have self empathy,

00:05:50.850 --> 00:05:52.552
which is extraordinary.

00:05:52.552 --> 00:05:53.152
All right.

00:05:53.186 --> 00:05:55.455
And this lack of empathy

00:05:55.621 --> 00:05:57.223
toward others in himself.

00:05:57.223 --> 00:05:58.591
You often see it in psychopaths.

00:05:58.591 --> 00:05:59.992
I'm not saying he's a psychopath,

00:05:59.992 --> 00:06:01.928
but it's such a curious

00:06:01.928 --> 00:06:03.763
combination of things.

00:06:03.763 --> 00:06:06.099
But, you know, he was

00:06:06.399 --> 00:06:08.067
a heroin addict

00:06:08.067 --> 00:06:12.372
and the heroin can can trigger

00:06:12.372 --> 00:06:13.706
this dissociation,

00:06:13.706 --> 00:06:16.008
this depersonalization syndrome.

00:06:16.008 --> 00:06:17.210
It's like you're living

00:06:18.177 --> 00:06:20.480
in a dream where you're watching yourself

00:06:21.848 --> 00:06:23.516
you can see this in schizophrenia

00:06:23.516 --> 00:06:25.351
and schizoaffective disorder,

00:06:25.351 --> 00:06:27.453
different psychiatric disorders

00:06:27.453 --> 00:06:29.088
where people feel separated

00:06:29.088 --> 00:06:29.722
from themselves.

00:06:29.722 --> 00:06:32.492
You see in people who take hallucinogens.

00:06:32.658 --> 00:06:33.393
Yes.

00:06:34.026 --> 00:06:35.628
And they were they tried.

00:06:35.628 --> 00:06:38.865
And so you sit in dream states,

00:06:38.865 --> 00:06:40.566
we measure all sorts of dreams

00:06:40.566 --> 00:06:42.101
or you see this.

00:06:42.101 --> 00:06:44.070
And so anybody who's had

00:06:44.070 --> 00:06:45.171
these strange dreams

00:06:45.171 --> 00:06:46.906
where they're hanging over themselves

00:06:46.906 --> 00:06:48.741
or an Anastasia.

00:06:48.741 --> 00:06:52.011
And so we people have experiences,

00:06:52.378 --> 00:06:53.513
but not all the time.

00:06:53.513 --> 00:06:56.449
It's not they don't feel that

00:06:56.449 --> 00:06:59.252
that it's occurring 100% of the time.

00:06:59.552 --> 00:07:00.453
In his case,

00:07:00.453 --> 00:07:00.987
it seems

00:07:00.987 --> 00:07:03.322
and he's living this all the time,

00:07:03.322 --> 00:07:05.358
like he's in a dream state

00:07:05.358 --> 00:07:07.293
and a very disturbing,

00:07:07.293 --> 00:07:08.861
very disturbing state.

00:07:08.861 --> 00:07:11.464
Well, Jim, thank you very much.

00:07:11.464 --> 00:07:13.199
He knows all the words.

00:07:13.199 --> 00:07:15.768
He knows he knows the he studied this.

00:07:15.935 --> 00:07:16.235
Right.

00:07:16.235 --> 00:07:16.769
That and that,

00:07:16.769 --> 00:07:18.104
I think, is the most bizarre part

00:07:18.104 --> 00:07:18.971
about it. Right.

00:07:18.971 --> 00:07:19.405
Is able

00:07:19.405 --> 00:07:20.973
to make that connection and able to study

00:07:20.973 --> 00:07:21.741
it all as well

00:07:21.741 --> 00:07:23.009
and choose

00:07:23.009 --> 00:07:24.777
that that entire path of learning.

00:07:24.777 --> 00:07:25.511
Thank you so much.

00:07:25.511 --> 00:07:26.646
I appreciate your time, Jim.

